  "limitations": [
    "Complete original Grand Lisboa exterior reconstructed from three inspected ordinary front/aerial photographs,retained OSM/Q1033099 outline and current standard viewer PMTiles/global terrain. No downloaded mesh,private photo texture,bespoke survey or archive research. Optical/furnished interiors,billboard imagery,exact decorative sculptures/artwork,panel inventory and surrounding city are excluded.",
    "The mapped54/55m parent outlines the lower casino/annex complex,not the whole261m landmark. Separate210m generalized hotel footprint aligns the rear shaft approximately east/west;the mirrored ovoid and entry face south. Retained261m total guides the crown/finial. Tower design origin is local[15.25,-12.25],internal rotation45degrees. Curved shaft/leaf/dome sections,seven reconstructed leaf tiers per side/front-back set,44 floor rows,side-annex/entrance dimensions and crown ornaments are photographic approximations,not an as-built architectural schedule.",
    "Detailed master preserves a narrow-waisted curved shaft,individual sweeping pointed leaf solids,glazing/floor bands,center ribs,ogive crown with diamond glazing band,globe and original open finial. Flattened ovoid casino uses geometric triangular mirrored cells with inset seams/recess returns;no dedicated texture atlas. Paired side drums/terraces,pointed front arch ribs,actual near foyer aperture and blank digital-sign pylon complete the exterior. Crown and finial ornament use original simplified geometry,not exact sculpture replicas. Far tiers aggregate facade/entrance detail while retaining the whole unique silhouette.",
    "Five existing shared256px graphs provide bronze/gold,window grid,polished stainless approximation of mirrored shell,painted-metal seams and granite foundation. A palette blank sign adds no image. Gold/silver/slate/cyan cell colors are original restrained patterns,not an exact panel-by-panel photographic copy. Shared reflective surfaces are stylized opaque materials. Portable fallback surfaces differ from bound viewer graphs. Source master and four authored browser tiers remain separate.",
    "Unmodified129x129/2m field oversamples one ordinary global terrain tile. Approximate base reference11m is rounded from its center;urban surface returns vary across the site. Podium/annex/pylon skirts and sampled individual arch-foot blocks embed below it;native ground remains visible through entry openings. The source does not flatten terrain or certify original street/foundation/accessibility/entry gradients. Curved facade depths,terrace/pool exclusions and exact site contact remain reconstructed. Estimated tier errors6/3/1.5/.7m are not certified mesh distances;physical laptop/phone and dense-city timing remain unmeasured."
  ],
